<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhongdu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1153–1215</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhongdu, the Central Capital, was the main capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a> from 1153 to 1215, on the site of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>. Enlarged from the earlier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> city by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wanyan-liang">Wanyan Liang</a>, it had grand palaces and walls. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> besieged and took it in 1215, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> later built his capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khanbaliq">Khanbaliq</a> to its north-east.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhongdu.jpg" alt="Zhongdu" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beijing_history.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
